# netsurf (MacSurf bridge): google's services and trending searches -- sheets in any document, real attribute lists, what a sanitizer walks
# Generated 2026-09-30
#
# After patches 168-169 google reported no errors, but its "Trending
# searches" stayed hidden. A temporary QuickJS throw trace (every Error at
# JS_Throw, with a backtrace built there; not committed) showed what its
# try/catch blocks had been swallowing:
#
# 1. `cannot read property 'insertRule' of null`, failing a chain of Wiz
#    services (SJpD2c <- HIg7cd <- PMS6Sd <- Sp69O). Closure's safe-CSS
#    builder (_.Sha) parses CSS through a <style> in
#    document.implementation.createHTMLDocument(''), and our `sheet`
#    getter answered null outside the main document. The bridge's
#    createHTMLDocument is a stand-in whose head/body/documentElement are
#    three detached elements, so nothing in it looked connected. Now: it
#    joins them and marks the root; `sheet` exists for an element in any
#    document.
# 2. Then `rule instanceof CSSStyleRule` was false: the polyfill runs again
#    when google's realm is rebuilt, and the second run replaced the CSSRule
#    classes while the `sheet` getter (installed only if missing) kept
#    making the first run's rules. The CSSOM section runs once per realm.
# 3. `not a function` in the trending component's render: Closure's HTML
#    sanitizer (_.Qc -> uQ) needs
#      scratchDoc.createRange().createContextualFragment(html)  (missing)
#      document.createTreeWalker(frag, 5, filter) with firstChild /
#        nextSibling / parentNode and FILTER_REJECT     (stubs returned null)
#      element.attributes, iterated to copy each element
#        (rebuilt from a fixed list of ~23 names: jsname, data-*, aria-*
#        and every other attribute were invisible)
#      new XMLSerializer().serializeToString(body)       (missing)
#
# macsurf_qjs.c: __attrNamesNative(el) -- the element's attribute names
# from its real namednodemap (the walk qjs_ih_serialize_attrs does).
# vita_polyfill.js:
# - attributes / getAttributeNames() over it: every attribute, in order,
#   iterable, attributes.getNamedItem / item / named access.
# - TreeWalker and NodeIterator per the DOM Standard (whatToShow, filter
#   function or {acceptNode}, ACCEPT/REJECT/SKIP; every traversal method);
#   NodeFilter constants.
# - Range.createContextualFragment (parsed through a <template>).
# - XMLSerializer.serializeToString (XHTML serialization: xmlns on the
#   root, `<br />`, &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; escaping).
# - the scratch document gets createDocumentFragment, createComment,
#   createElementNS, createRange, createTreeWalker, createNodeIterator,
#   importNode and createEvent from the main document.
# Test: JS-sanitize.html 7/7 (the expected strings are Chromium's; the
# TreeWalker/NodeIterator/XMLSerializer code itself was also run in
# Chromium against the same cases: 7/7).
# Sim: google.com shows its Trending searches list (the rows were built in
# the DOM but hidden: the component shows the list only after render, and
# render threw inside the sanitizer).
